========================================================================================
WHAT A DEGREE-d PHASE ORACLE CAN CONCENTRATE
========================================================================================
  P(x) ~ sin^2(phi(x)/2). Perfect concentration needs phi to approximate
  pi * 1[x = x*], so this is the approximate degree of an indicator.
  Enhancement is 2^n P(x*); 1.0 is uniform, 2^n is a delta function.

     n    2^n       d=1       d=2       d=3       d=4       d=5
  -------------------------------------------------------------
     3      8      4.00      7.00      8.00         -         -
     4     16      5.00     11.00     15.00     16.00         -
     5     32      6.00     16.00     26.00     31.00     32.00
     6     64      7.00     22.00     42.00     57.00     63.00

  (2) A PHASE LINEAR IN THE ENERGY — the shipped drift. Best achievable
      enhancement when phi is CONSTRAINED to phi = lambda (E - E_bar),
      optimised over lambda, on random landscapes.
     n    2^n   best enh  at lambda  deg-n free
  ---------------------------------------------
     3      8       3.86       0.01        8.00
     4     16       5.66       0.01       16.00
     5     32       2.99       0.01       32.00
     6     64       4.71       0.01       64.00

  The first table is the capability of the circuit family by degree; the
  second is what the SHIPPED drift can reach, since its phase is linear in
  E by construction. A large gap between the two columns of table (2) is
  the price of using a Boltzmann-shaped phase instead of a threshold one,
  and it is a theorem about polynomials rather than a property of any
  mixer, schedule or shot budget.
